nia at birth. Later, they showed ataxia, nystagmus, and dysarthria.
Psychomotor development was delayed. Bilateral cataracts were
operated in the first decade of life. Patients had a progressive clin-
ical course with stabilization at different ages and severity. Muscle
involvement was predominant in the proximal and distal muscles
of the lower limbs. Scoliosis and deformity of the hands and feet
bones were present in four patients. Serum creatine kinase levels
were moderately increased. Patients had hypergonadotropic hypog-
onadism and mild to severe mental retardation. Electromyography
and muscle biopsy showed myopathic features. Muscle CT showed
severe fat degeneration of the posterior thoracic and pelvic mus-
cles, and almost all thigh muscles. On the legs the peroneus and
posterior compartment muscles were severely degenerated. Brain
MRI showed severe atrophy of the vermis and cerebellar hemi-
spheres. Patients were homozygous for a four base duplication in
exon 6 (c.506_509dupAAGA).
