fibre predominance. 29 Pts. were homozygous or compound het-
erozygous for N88K; 10 Pts. had mutations in the promoter
region; 7 Pts. harboured 8 previously unreported mutations,
including 4 missense mutations, 1 splice-site mutation, 2 dele-
tions, and 1 promoter region mutation. Except for the promoter
mutation, no consistent phenotype-genotype correlations were
detected.
