presenting with the complex syndrome of slowly progressive
parkinsonism, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis and dementia were
completely examined clinically, including neuropsychological
examination, and they were assessed using EMG and EP . Blood
and CSF samples were also examined, and the levels of inflamma-
tory and neurodegenerative markers (beta-amyloid, cystatin C and
tau-proteins) were established.
